  "pllGuideIntro": "From the front and right sides alone you can name any PLL. Read the six stickers along the top, left to right, and look for the features below, in order. The first that matches decides the group; then find the line in the group that fits.",
  "pllGuideTermsTitle": "The words",
  "pllTermThreeBar": "One side is all one colour.",
  "pllTermHeadlights": "Two corners of a side are one colour, with a different edge between them.",
  "pllTermBar": "Two stickers of a side next to each other are one colour. Inside means it is next to the middle of the strip, outside means it is at an end.",
  "pllTermBookends": "The two outermost stickers, the first and the last, are one colour.",
  "pllTermChecker": "Two colours take turns, four or five stickers in a row.",
  "pllTermColoursTitle": "Adjacent and opposite",
  "pllTermColours": "Colours are compared on the cube: opposite colours are on opposite faces (white and yellow, say), and any other two different colours are adjacent.",
  "pllGuideOrderTitle": "The order to look in",
  "pllGuideOrder": "1. A 3-bar.\n2. Headlights.\n3. A 2-bar.\n4. Bookends.",
  "pllGuideMirrorTitle": "Mirror images",
  "pllGuideMirror": "Every picture counts mirrored too: if it only fits when you read the six stickers from right to left, use the line as if it were drawn that way round.",
  "pllGuideLetterTitle": "Which letter?",
  "pllGuideLetter": "Where a line names two cases, such as Ua and Ub, it shows both. They are told apart by which way round the pattern is: the one drawn as it is in the picture, or its mirror image. Two lines need one more look:",
  "pllGuideLetterU": "3-bar with headlights (U), 3-bar on the left: if the edge on the right is opposite the 3-bar's colour it is Ua, if it is opposite the headlights' colour it is Ub. With the 3-bar on the right it is the other way round.",
  "pllGuideLetterA": "Both bars inside, bookends match (A): if the bookends' colour is adjacent to the bars' colour it is Aa, if it is opposite it is Ab.",
  "pllGuideCredit": "After Mark49152's Two-Sided PLL Recognition Guide.",
  "trainerTabRules": "Patterns",
  "trainerTabAuf": "AUF",
  "trainerTermsInfo": "The words",
  "pllAufIntro": "AUF (Adjust U Face) is the last turn of the top layer that lines it up once the PLL is done. Which way to turn has no fixed answer per case: it depends on the algorithm you use. For many cases the patterns make it obvious; these are the hints for the less obvious ones.",
  "pllAufUTitle": "U: the 2:1 pattern",
  "pllAufU1": "The odd edge is the opposite colour: the 3-bar is adjacent.",
  "pllAufU2": "The odd edge is an adjacent colour: the 3-bar is opposite.",
  "pllAufGbdTitle": "Gb/d: opposite lights",
  "pllAufGbd": "The 2-bar touches the side with the 2:1 pattern.",
  "pllAufJTitle": "J: double 2-bar",
  "pllAufJ": "The 3-bar is next to the side whose colours are adjacent.",
  "pllAufATitle": "A: double 2-bar",
  "pllAufA": "The lights are next to the side whose colours are adjacent.",
  "pllAufRGacTitle": "R and Ga/c: bookends",
  "pllAufR": "R: the lights are further from the test pair.",
  "pllAufGac": "Ga/c: the lights are nearer to the test pair.",
  "pllAufFTitle": "F: checkers",
  "pllAufF": "The bar is next to the pair of opposite colours."
